    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah i get that. but if most of the \"liberty\" arguments are actually based on debunked info or stuff that goes against consensus medical advice, doesnt that make the \"legitimate philosophical concern\" part kind of a stretch? like, if the foundation is wrong, can the argument even be considered valid anymore?",
